      "message": "This is safe and public but reads the object a raw `Value` points to, and a `Value` is only valid until the next allocation. The `Cx` methods that take one are `pub unsafe fn`, and the check it wraps, `Vm::is_other` (vm.rs:1037), is `pub(crate)`. In safe code, a `Value` held across a collection makes it read a freed and reused block: a vector\u0027s `Value`, dropped, collected, then 64 ipairs allocated, reads as an ipair. 1260921 keeps this as a raw `get` inside the same safe fn.\n\nNothing outside the crate calls it, so `pub(crate)` is enough. Otherwise make it `pub unsafe fn` with a Safety section.",
